Perfect — now we connect everything you built into a **real working flow**. This is where it all clicks. 🔥

You have:

```text
Spring Boot app (Producer + Consumer)
NATS server (running)
JetStream (enabled)
```

Now you need to **trigger the producer via HTTP**.

---

# 🚀 WHAT YOU NEED TO DO

You will send an HTTP request like this:

```text
POST → your Spring Boot API → publishes to NATS → consumer reads it
```

---

# 🧱 STEP 1 — Make Sure App is Running

When you start your app, you should see:

```text
Tomcat started on port 8080
```

👉 This means:

```text
Your API is live at: http://localhost:8080
```

---

# 🧱 STEP 2 — Endpoint You Created

From your code:

```java
@RequestMapping("/orders")
@PostMapping
```

👉 Final API:

```text
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
```

---

# 🧱 STEP 3 — Request Body (VERY IMPORTANT)

You must send JSON matching your `OrderDTO`.

---

## ✅ Correct JSON Body

```json
{
  "customerName": "Tanya",
  "orderId": 101,
  "items": ["Pen", "Notebook"]
}
```

---

# 🧱 STEP 4 — How to Send Request

---

## 👉 Option 1 — Postman (Recommended)

1. Open Postman
2. Select **POST**
3. Enter URL:

```text
http://localhost:8080/orders
```

4. Go to **Body → raw → JSON**
5. Paste:

```json
{
  "customerName": "Tanya",
  "orderId": 101,
  "items": ["Pen", "Notebook"]
}
```

6. Click **Send**

---

## 👉 Option 2 — cURL (Terminal)

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/orders \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d "{\"customerName\":\"Tanya\",\"orderId\":101,\"items\":[\"Pen\",\"Notebook\"]}"
```

---

# 🧠 WHAT WILL HAPPEN INTERNALLY

---

## 🔥 Flow

```text
HTTP Request
    ↓
OrderController
    ↓
OrderPublisher
    ↓
NATS (orders.created)
    ↓
JetStream Stream (ORDERS)
    ↓
OrderConsumer
    ↓
Console log
```

---

# ✅ EXPECTED OUTPUT

---

## 👉 In your **Spring Boot logs**

### Producer:

```text
Published Order: {...}
```

---

### Consumer:

```text
Consumed Order: OrderDTO(...)
```

---

# ❗ IF YOU DON’T SEE CONSUMER LOGS

Then check:

### 1. NATS server running?

```text
nats-server running on 4222
```

---

### 2. Stream exists?

```powershell
.\nats.exe stream info ORDERS
```

---

### 3. Subject match?

```text
orders.created
```

---

# 🧠 COMMON MISTAKES (VERY IMPORTANT)

---

## ❌ Wrong JSON

```json
{
  "name": "Tanya"
}
```

👉 Will fail (fields don’t match DTO)

---

## ❌ Wrong URL

```text
http://localhost:8080/order   ❌
```

Correct:

```text
http://localhost:8080/orders  ✅
```

---

## ❌ Consumer not started

If your `@PostConstruct` fails → no logs

